The lengths in a right-angled triangle satisfy $c^2=a^2+b^2$, where $c$ is the longest side. Find $b$ when $c=13$ cm and $a=5$ cm.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,draw=black,text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont]
\draw (0,0)--(4,0)--(0,2)--cycle;
\draw (0.25,0)--(0.25,0.25)--(0,0.25);
\path (2,0) node[below] {$b$};
\path (0,1) node[left] {$a=5\text{ cm}$};
\path (2,1) node[above right] {$c=13\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
